  "description_html": "Skeletal reconstruction of the therizinosaur <i>Enigmosaurus mongoliensis</i>, known from its holotype <b>IGM 100/84</b>. The remains were unearthed from the Bayan Shireh Formation, in Mongolia.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Barsbold1983_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Barsbold1983-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> It has an estimated length of 5 m (16 ft) with a weight ranging from 454 to 907 kg (1,001 to 2,000 lb)<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, although it is commonly known from the pelvis, other body remains were labelled as <b>IGM 100/84</b>, however, definitive assignment of these fossils to the holotype are yet unclear.<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>",
